# Depends-On: niri-0wd0-vertical-layout.patch
# Title: Add main-axis-independent physical direction actions
#
# Adds focus-left/right/up/down and move-left/right/up/down actions whose
# direction remains aligned with the physical screen on both horizontal and
# vertical scrolling layouts.
diff --git a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Key-Bindings.md b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Key-Bindings.md
--- a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Key-Bindings.md
+++ b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Key-Bindings.md
@@ -97,6 +97,8 @@
 
 These examples assume the default horizontal main axis. The action names stay the same with `layout.main-axis "vertical"`, but their physical direction follows the main/cross-axis interpretation of the layout.
 
+To keep directional key bindings aligned with the physical screen direction regardless of the main axis, use `focus-left`, `focus-right`, `focus-up`, and `focus-down`. The corresponding move actions are `move-left`, `move-right`, `move-up`, and `move-down`.
+
 Similarly, you can bind touchpad scroll "ticks".
 Touchpad scrolling is continuous, so for these binds it is split into discrete intervals based on distance travelled.
 
